A component the build cannot inline -- `card` sits under a dynamic `for` --
whose own body holds a reactive `if`. So the instance carries its own slot
renderer, and three separate things about that were wrong in both Go platforms
on this one program.

The nodes that renderer creates have to be discovered. Both platforms walked
every component's *body* and every func the *Model* emits, which is not the same
set: `__renderSlot0` belongs to the instance. So the label inside the reactive
block had no spec on fyne -- `container.Add(__n1)` against a variable no
statement declared -- and no declaration on gtk4, which stopped the build
outright with `gtk4: no widget for node "GtkLabel"`.

The box the renderer renders into has to exist. gtk4 set `c.__root = nil` and
appended into it; it builds the box now, as fyne's sibling already did.

And the box has to be reachable from what the instance renders as. Both
platforms chose Root from the widgets no AppendChild consumed, and the slot's
subtree is built into `__root` rather than named by a ref -- so `__root` was in
no list and its whole subtree was invisible: `c.Root = c.__n0`. The translator
records it when it meets the call that renders it, which is why the *order*
below is part of the claim: `container.NewVBox(c.__n0, c.__root)` and the two
`BoxAppend`s in that sequence are the position the slot was written, not an
append after the fact.

deny out/go/fyne/model.go `if c.open \{\n\t\tcontainer.Add\(__n1\)` -- the renderer declares the label before adding it; going straight to the Add is what a node with no spec left behind
deny out/go/gtk4/model.go `c.__root = nil` -- the instance's slot renders into a box, so the box is built before the first render appends into it
deny out/go/fyne/model.go `c.Root = c.__n0` -- Root is the whole instance, box included; the button alone leaves the slot's subtree unreachable
deny out/go/gtk4/model.go `c.Root = c.__n0` -- same claim in gtk4's vocabulary: Root is the box holding both, not the one widget nothing consumed

-- app.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"

output {
    go {
        fyne
        gtk4(gir="builtin")
    }
}

component card(name = "") node {
    var open = true
    button(text=name, @click { open = !open })
    if open {
        text(value="body of " + name)
    }
}

component main node {
    var items list[string] = ["a", "b"]
    for var it = items {
        card(name=it)
    }
}

window {
    main
}
